" <C-c><C-c> (org#dispatch#ctrl_c) picks the action for the line under the cursor.

Given org (closed CLOCK line: recalculate):
  CLOCK: [2026-07-01 mié 09:00]--[2026-07-01 mié 10:30] =>  0:00

Execute:
  call org#dispatch#ctrl_c()
  let d = Date(2026, 7, 1)
  AssertEqual 'CLOCK: [' . d . ' 09:00]--[' . d . ' 10:30] =>  1:30', getline(1)

Given org (open CLOCK line: clock out):
  * Task
    :LOGBOOK:
    CLOCK: START
    :END:

Execute:
  call setline(3, '  CLOCK: ' . Now())
  3
  call org#dispatch#ctrl_c()
  AssertEqual '  CLOCK: ' . Now() . '--' . Now() . ' =>  0:00', getline(3)

Given org (checkbox line: toggle and update the cookie):
  * List [0/1]
  - [ ] a

Execute:
  2
  call org#dispatch#ctrl_c()

Expect org:
  * List [1/1]
  - [X] a

Given org (stale day name on a timestamp line: fix it):
  * Task
    SCHEDULED: <2026-09-29 xxx 10:00 +1w>

Execute:
  2
  call org#dispatch#ctrl_c()
  AssertEqual '  SCHEDULED: <' . Date(2026, 9, 29) . ' 10:00 +1w>', getline(2)

Given org (nothing to do: the buffer is unchanged):
  * Task
  plain text

Execute:
  2
  call org#dispatch#ctrl_c()

Expect org:
  * Task
  plain text
